# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-21: compiler and platform macros
of the config macro review.

# Decided
- trueqbit (a): SQLITE_ORM_COMPILER_<maker>_<compiler> and
  SQLITE_ORM_PLATFORM_<platform>, after compiler.h / platform.h - every
  public tier carries a marker. Weighed and rejected: Boost.Predef's
  COMP_/OS_/PLAT_ (from memory; it files Android under PLAT, and UNIX as a
  family fits neither), and leaving them bare.
- trueqbit settles the open alias question (dissent of ca2c2970 closed):
  no hypothetical backward-compatibility macros. Someone using an
  undocumented guard switches to the new name when upgrading, unless a
  complicated multi-version setup; addressed once it becomes a problem.
  SQLITE_ORM_OMITS_CODECVT keeps its alias - a real contract.

